  "title": "The Sign at Knee Height",
  "family": "fiction",
  "category": "positive public good",
  "premise": "A park volunteer wants all visitors to find a small puppet show, but the only direction sign is hidden behind a crowd’s shoulders. They add a second matching sign on a clear low stand and a visible path symbol, allowing both tall and short cartoon visitors to follow the same route.",
  "hook": "The directions disappear when everyone arrives.",
  "visible_action": "Crowd gathers; overhead sightline blocks; low sign slides into open view; matching ground symbols lead to the puppet stage.",
  "intended_takeaway_or_theme": "Check an instruction from more than one viewpoint.",
  "gate": "Do not claim accessibility compliance from a cartoon; real public signage requires relevant standards and user testing.",
